{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And Elohim said, Let there be light</b> — The word 'said' here serves to indicate will and desire, as in 'Whatsoever thy soul desireth, I will do for thee' (1 Samuel 20:4) — whatever you desire and desire, and similarly 'and let her be a wife to your master's son, as HaShem has spoken' (Genesis 24:51) — as He desired; for such was the will before Him. Or it is like thought, as in 'she said in her heart' (Isaiah 47:8); 'and the leaders of Judah said in their hearts' (Zechariah 12:5). And the meaning is to say that there was no toil or effort. And thus our Rabbis called this 'thought'; they said: Thought — by day; Deed — at twilight. And this is to indicate a deliberate matter that has reason and purpose, not a simple desire alone. And the word of הויה (havayah, existence-verb) indicates an act of standing time, as in 'and thou wouldst be a king unto them' (Nehemiah 6:6). Therefore Scripture says that when He created the material of the heavens, He said that from that material there should be a radiant thing, and called it light." "<b>And there was light</b> — It does not say 'and it was so,' as is said regarding the other days, because the light did not remain in this arrangement all the days, unlike the rest of the work of Creation. And our Rabbis have a midrash on this in a hidden sod. And know that the days mentioned in the work of Creation were, in the creation of the heavens and the earth, actual days, composed of hours and moments, and there were six like the six days of the work of Creation, according to the plain sense of Scripture. And in the inner meaning of the matter they are called 'days' for the sefirot emanated from above, for every utterance that produces havyah is called a 'day.' And they were six, 'for to YHWH belong greatness and might.' And the utterances were ten, for in the first ones the name 'day' does not apply. And the explanation in the arrangement of the verses on this matter is exalted and hidden, and our knowledge of it is less than a drop from the great sea."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-21T22:11:59.970006572Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}